  More like you got one question answered and immediately came back 
with another.  On the other hand, if you put a number of questions 
together in a single post, often you'll only get one or two answered.


  I think the main problem is that Nethack has thousand rules, a
thousand exceptions, and a thousand tricks.

  So if you keep asking questions one at a time, one right after
another it will take a lot of work on the part of other people if they
decide to answer them.

  So be aware that if you ask many questions and don't give the
impression you're trying to find the answers on your own, then people
here will feel that they're being taken advantage of.

  The best approach is to show that you've put some effort into trying
to find out the answer.  "What does a ring of free action do?" won't
get nearly as good a response as:

  "I have a ring of free action, but I wore it and a cockatrice still
did me in. What am I doing wrong?"

  Or maybe:

  "I got grabbed and my ring of free action didn't get me loose.  What
did I do wrong?"

  Or even:

  "I have a ring of free action.  Will that help me in <some
situation>?"

  All teachers appreciate effort on the part of the student.  And the
teachers here work for free.  So if you want help, it's probably best
to try and keep people happy.


  Of course, all that is just my opinion.




